course: dictionary
lesson: 488
title: Going up: the word ascension
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An ascension is the act of rising or going up. «The ascension of the balloon took it high above the trees» means the balloon floated up into the sky.
explain: In church and Bible stories, the Ascension is a special event. Christians believe Jesus was taken up into heaven forty days after Easter. «Forty days after Easter Jesus was taken up into heaven; this is called the Ascension.» The capital A shows it is one particular event.
explain: Use the clues around the word. Words like «taken up» and «into heaven» show the meaning is about going upward. Check it by swapping in your meaning: «Forty days after Easter Jesus was taken up into heaven; this is called the going up.» It still makes sense.
fact: Ascension means rising or going up.
fact: «The Ascension» with a capital A is a special event in the Christian church.
fact: Christians believe Jesus rose from the dead at Easter, then went up into heaven forty days later at the Ascension.
fact: Ascension Day is a Christian feast day. The story is told in the Gospel of Luke and the Acts of the Apostles.
fact: Ascension can also mean coming to a high position, such as a king coming to the throne, but «accession» is the more usual word for that. Ascension Island is a small island in the Atlantic Ocean.
exercise: «Forty days after Easter Jesus was taken up into heaven; this is called the Ascension.» What is the Ascension? | A small island in the Atlantic | A kind of Easter egg hunt | *A church event when Christians believe Jesus went up into heaven | A party with balloons and games
exercise: «The ascension of the balloon took it high above the trees.» What does ascension mean here? | *Going up | Falling asleep | Coming down to land | Being painted a bright colour
exercise: Ascension Day is a Christian feast day. What kind of day is it? | A day when the sun goes down early | A day for building sandcastles | *A special day in the church calendar | A day for school holidays only
test: «The crowds cheered at the ascension of the new king to the throne.» What does ascension mean here? | Lots of cheering only | Falling asleep in the sun | *Coming to a high position, such as the throne | Going down a hill
test: What is the best way to check the meaning of an unknown word? | Skip it forever and never look back | Count the letters | Ask a friend to guess | *Swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense
exam: Which word means nearly the same as ascension? | *Rising | Descent | Sinking | Landing
